[2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556616} {:answer/id #uuid "65032a8d-a4f3-517c-a748-1a00ee1aed26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup [2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556663} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba2ca60-ef41-5208-8e4e-1de935cdae6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556810} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b0992f-1500-5142-a5f8-a0f17e4f6976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556907} {:answer/id #uuid "d7976712-61bc-5824-bdde-76934e8b24a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556963}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186556907} :answer-field/id #uuid "2435bb7a-799d-59f0-ad2e-0c6284676d40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e377c474-d1b6-5e34-ae2e-6bda298c1707" :question/math-academy-id "q-28966" :question/problem "Find all the values of $x$ that satisfy $3x+5>11$ or $2x-3\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $3x+5>11:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5 & >11 \\\\ 3x & >6 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/87/87831ea65f4caa557c8e8826faaa43a60737c3590393872902818921668787d0.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2x-3\\le 1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/49/4965930532798f18907e5319f2fd9fe5f17d9c1969c12d9795f9867a2cb13351.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/a9/a9543d5a2add249d869a667d16bea75780b0e44e4c0d2bde2cf460733d5e9634.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 2$ or $x>2.$ We can write this using interval notation as\n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9920cd70-713b-5652-a589-462984092c55" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557380}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557402 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4208aa5a-ebcf-544c-bdab-57c640b053b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556576} {:answer/id #uuid "4fac84c7-58d6-5175-a114-10e9acc01ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (10,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556607} {:answer/id #uuid "a9701182-7d89-5629-8529-d4fad7cef8ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-10)\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556850} {:answer/id #uuid "e67b06b1-5b7a-5ce7-a2e3-c9ca5a45bf11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-10,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556998} {:answer/id #uuid "f052b297-ca34-569f-a527-057e0db288ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557022} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa95610-12f2-5abb-9640-0c55094b614f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49cc684c-6a61-5a0a-9979-944836444765" :question/math-academy-id "q-25402" :question/problem "Find all the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x-5>1$ or $2x-7<13.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $2x-5>1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & >1 \\\\ 2x & >6 \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/20/2048d360b427cfd94e92a16f7b9f8cd9ca9c88e808bf3b6205d60eebd71aa1cf.png)\n\nThen, we solve $2x-7<13:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-7 & <13 \\\\ 2x & <20 \\\\ x & <10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c1/c1a63d1c991f309dbc10a89f0416c910c2c31bde5fdf069682a6127a1f66987a.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/e0/e03d04e5d2d5d571f5b80353081253087f99b2bf58fd86ae56eff3af26415b92.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x<10$ or $x>3.$ We can write this using interval notation as $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"} :step/id #uuid "e397555c-38d7-597d-9eef-be097531f336" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557343}}] :activity/title "Compound OR Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556419}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573977} :activity/id #uuid "7a5b4a5d-3859-51ba-9332-c80d1a470485" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050680 :topic/id #uuid "5e676adf-aa45-5e67-b4e5-57ec40661f6e" :topic/math-academy-id 1576} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573960 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d22ef26-67e9-570b-ae16-d5566bfb5791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- ∞, 0]∪(2, 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114374} {:answer/id #uuid "c20ac221-36b1-5a2b-ad46-804b7ae65441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- ∞, 0)∪[2, 4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114375} {:answer/id #uuid "d101d38d-df01-5802-bb76-36b9e5304387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "[0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114376} {:answer/id #uuid "21a3f80c-87a9-5b22-ad7d-760b970bd83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- ∞, 2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114377} {:answer/id #uuid "4250dcb6-c304-54c4-972d-d553943e333d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- ∞, 4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114378}] :answer-field/id #uuid "44ac194c-0973-53bd-953a-017fa40875eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "657ccae9-03d3-59e9-af36-01df6031e4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-59512" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-3 \\le 2x - 7 \\le 1$ or $2 + 3x < 2$."} :step/id #uuid "45728fdf-d05f-50d8-8c7d-444c58d427ec" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573980}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573977 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213b086c-9de7-5968-8df0-bfcd9ec886ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No real solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573462} {:answer/id #uuid "2301e2ab-92a9-51b4-a9b3-3aba28597748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a8/a889f5a6049842727a00007f29e7e0934a6edac45544f969b2596d43bdc16806.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573466} {:answer/id #uuid "707333ba-3177-5631-8eb1-ce18a0823c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bc/bc475f69877ff3ae14e78430698b5a8a80f9a422c58a5558f08a2e34aff7efae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573564} {:answer/id #uuid "a58948ab-e814-5339-8ea6-362b2133ac35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d9/d9f61f95d32f5f856494ed5e6327bd7101237b906ecf7b90125b746b4a6fa383.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573637} {:answer/id #uuid "b62d3b29-26a8-5c24-8540-fcd3da4394c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4d/4d8b75381554b4fefbe3b89abe5a8a9604036e4ccdda3b9cd53f61fd6df7f462.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573662}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573662} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55d58ab-6f36-570d-8c9d-3ef2320bbe2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e93fe40f-a4aa-5acf-8d5c-2ac8fa4691b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-25487" :question/problem "Which of the following number lines represents the values of $w$ that satisfy $3w-7\\le 5$ or $5w+7\\ge -3$, or $2w<8?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $3w-7\\le 5:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3w-7 & \\le 5 \\\\ 3w & \\le 12 \\\\ w & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/df/dfbf9fce10352e640bb62b75c49339e54c3d22b918e2dfb60a72472ef5129639.png)\n\nThen, we solve $5w+7\\ge -3:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5w+7 & \\ge -3 \\\\ 5w & \\ge -10 \\\\ w & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/53/535934975bf21706e8bfa3b54fa51a0f344f585e89f3003ad042f6fb660c3441.png)\n\nFinally, we solve $2w<8:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2w & <8 \\\\ w & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ba/ba806ca20f496c724c4411c282ab44d81d7713c7b8635b3c286faff1d7728f20.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $w$ that satisfy at least one of the inequalities, we overlay the three graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/f0/f084c11e4faf4fdcfc69a32900bf62c1bddfa2266007f8f4ddecf8ab928230fa.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty <w<\\infty .$"} :step/id #uuid "e49fe02b-c6f2-5520-b855-c1be08e7b33d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573960}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573980 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb6a318-faf2-5363-9952-257a1853b996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/44/44b4a08bd4b2aade4c86ac1845878dc44cb41a2fd84cb36c19cfd8110bd84f61.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573484} {:answer/id #uuid "53529ee0-0323-5186-834b-402cd87e5b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6a/6a34e6d82defce5f47d5562151a5ccfe88d4475f60c33632950ff109e4fc2460.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573526} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1a84ac-dd61-54df-9d04-2d6ecbc519cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8a/8ade78ec1b4adac7ee63d1eb3e5b5cc82ffe5b00437add005b7824dc2e0c05a9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573581} {:answer/id #uuid "83e558d1-2de8-5cb9-b43e-dacc90324e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c8/c82330c4ccd9aff01ac73cd1ebac56d50f685e0da258fb83ec619ebd11023694.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573597} {:answer/id #uuid "f00f0e95-02eb-5786-8fec-b2276b3ddcc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/72/72edfbf24542f84652d24d879c2298cff603f960a22885e0b8856635a80d201c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573744} :answer-field/id #uuid "d394b718-d2f3-5360-aead-3ecf50fe63f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2564ad9-789a-55f4-bf0e-d5069f16525a" :question/math-academy-id "q-76087" :question/problem "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-2\\le 2x-6\\le 4$ or $12x-22<14?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $-2\\le 2x-6\\le 4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\le 2x-6\\le 4 \\\\ 4 & \\le 2x\\le 10 \\\\ 2 & \\le x\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/c8/c82330c4ccd9aff01ac73cd1ebac56d50f685e0da258fb83ec619ebd11023694.png)\n\nThen, we solve $12x-22<14:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-22 & <14 \\\\ 12x & <36 \\\\ x & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8a/8ade78ec1b4adac7ee63d1eb3e5b5cc82ffe5b00437add005b7824dc2e0c05a9.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/72/72edfbf24542f84652d24d879c2298cff603f960a22885e0b8856635a80d201c.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 5.$"} :step/id #uuid "fefec9ef-1682-5b4f-ba9e-308af8f3441f"}] :activity/title "Compound OR Inequalities" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573416}]}
